            "review_title": "Review at Stone Castle Cafe",
            "review_text": "Larry G\nWashington DC, District of Columbia56 contributions\n0\nPleasant and Interesting for Coffee or Dining\nDec 2016 • Solo\nMy party of three enjoyed their lunches. The prices are fine and my Bo Kho Banh Mi (beef stew with fresh baguette) was flavorful. There are gardens and terraces to explore or use. It isn't on the beaten path and the main road is divided by a sewer canal so you might miss the place from the other side of the road. It isn't far from Dam Sen Park so it might be a nice place to end the day. But I wouldn't go too far afield because there are so many equally interesting restaurants in the city.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 5, 2017",
